package seo

const ServerVersion = "0.1.0"

const RegistryName = "si.openany/seo"

const RegistryTitle = "Google Keyword Checker"

const RegistryDescription = "Keyword research via DataForSEO: Google/Bing volume, difficulty, ideas, ranked keywords, SERP."

const Endpoint = "https://seo.openany.si"

// Instructions is the model-facing server description. It names only the four
// SEO tools. Catalog browsing tools stay on the root MCP.
const Instructions = "Google Keyword Checker looks up keyword research through DataForSEO only. Tools: keyword_research (Google or Bing search volume, and Google keyword difficulty), keyword_ideas (new or related Google terms for an article or landing page), ranked_keywords (Google keywords a domain or page currently ranks for), serp_overview (Google or Bing page-1 organic results). Use when the user asks whether a keyword is worth pursuing for search traffic, wants keyword ideas, wants a domain's current rankings, or wants page-1 competitors. Triggers include SEO, search volume, keyword difficulty, keyword ideas, ranked keywords, SERP, 选题, 落地页该用什么词, and \"is this keyword worth it\". A call without confirm returns the current published price and does not call the paid gateway. Call again with the same arguments, confirm true, and that price_version only after the user confirms the price. A displayed price is not a price lock. Execution needs the caller's OpenAny API key on the connection as Authorization: Bearer <key>. Create a key at https://openany.si/dashboard?page=api-keys and store it in the client's secure settings. Never ask the user to paste the key into chat. This server has no OAuth flow and does not collect secrets with form elicitation. If execution_state is unknown after a timeout, do not retry automatically. Do NOT use for Xiaohongshu, Douyin, TikTok, Weibo, or other social listening. Do NOT claim backlinks, Domain Rating, Ahrefs, Semrush, Serper, or Tavily. Ranked keywords are Google-only in v1. This server does not browse a catalog and does not run arbitrary APIs."

const KeywordResearchDescription = "Looks up Google or Bing search volume and, on Google, keyword difficulty (KD) via DataForSEO. Google uses DataForSEO Labs Keyword Overview, which returns search volume and keyword difficulty together. Bing uses DataForSEO Bing search volume only; keyword difficulty is not available for Bing in v1. Optional include_trend adds DataForSEO Labs Historical Keyword Data for volume history of the same keywords. That history is not new-keyword discovery. Use when the user asks whether a keyword or topic is worth writing for search traffic, wants search volume, keyword difficulty, monthly searches, organic demand, 选题, 有没有人搜, 难不难, or \"is this keyword worth it\". Example asks: \"How many people search this term in the US each month, and how hard is it?\" / \"「email finder API」在美国值得做吗？每月有多少人搜、难不难？\" Returns search volume and, for Google, keyword difficulty. Monthly history is returned only when include_trend is true. Does not return page-1 competitor lists (use serp_overview), new keyword ideas (use keyword_ideas), or the keywords a domain currently ranks for (use ranked_keywords). Do NOT use for social listening. Do NOT claim backlinks, Domain Rating, Ahrefs, Semrush, Serper, or Tavily. Before any paid call, returns the current price with is_quote false and does not call the gateway until confirm is true and price_version matches."

const KeywordIdeasDescription = "Returns related or category-relevant Google keyword ideas via DataForSEO Labs, for an article, personal site, or landing page. Use when the user wants new keyword ideas, related keywords, \"what else should I target\", 还该加哪些词, 落地页该用什么词, or content ideation from seed terms or a site URL. If the user gives seed keywords, mode ideas (default) uses Google Keyword Ideas and mode related uses Google SERP \"searches related to\" for the first seed only. If the user gives only a site, this uses Keywords For Site: terms relevant to that domain or page, not the keywords it currently ranks for. Example asks: \"What keywords should I add to this article?\" / \"What words should my landing page use?\" / \"还有哪些我没想到、但跟我们产品同类的新词也可以做？\" Returns the related keywords and the search volume or competition fields present in the DataForSEO response. Do NOT use to look up volume or keyword difficulty for a keyword the user already has (use keyword_research). Do NOT use for the keywords a domain currently ranks for and their positions (use ranked_keywords). Do NOT use for who is on page 1 (use serp_overview). Google only in v1. Do NOT claim backlinks, Domain Rating, Ahrefs, Semrush, Serper, or Tavily, and do not treat a rising volume trend as a newly discovered term. The current price is returned first; the paid call runs only after confirm and a matching price_version."

const RankedKeywordsDescription = "Returns the Google keywords that a domain, subdomain, or page currently ranks for, with position and available search volume, via DataForSEO Labs Ranked Keywords. Use when the user asks which keywords a site is ranking for, \"what are we ranking for\", 目前排在前面的词, or wants a competitor's current ranking keywords, especially page-1 or top positions. target is a domain or page URL. historical_serp_mode defaults to live current rankings. positions limits results to rank_group less than or equal to that number; 10 means page 1. Example asks: \"Which keywords does example.com currently rank for in the US, especially on page 1?\" / \"oursite.com 现在排在前面的是哪些词？\" Returns the target's ranking keywords, approximate position, and available search volume. Does not return lost rankings unless historical_serp_mode is lost or all. Do NOT use for the highest-volume related terms of a topic (use keyword_ideas). Do NOT use for who appears on page 1 for one keyword (use serp_overview). This tool is Google-only in v1. Do NOT claim Bing ranked keywords. Do NOT claim backlinks, Domain Rating, Ahrefs, Semrush, Serper, or Tavily. The current price is returned first; the paid call runs only after confirm and a matching price_version."

const SERPOverviewDescription = "Returns Google or Bing page-1 SERP results and organic competitors via DataForSEO. Use when the user asks who ranks for a keyword, wants SERP analysis, page-one competitors, \"who is on page 1\", or whether to write a new page or update an existing one. Example asks: \"Who ranks on page 1 for this keyword?\" / \"这些词的第一页现在是谁？我该写新文章，还是改现有落地页？\" Returns page-1 organic rank, title, and URL. depth is fixed at 10 so the call is one SERP page. Do NOT use for search volume or keyword difficulty alone (use keyword_research). Do NOT use for a domain's current ranking keywords (use ranked_keywords). Do NOT use for new keyword ideas (use keyword_ideas). Do NOT claim backlinks, Domain Rating, Ahrefs, Semrush, Serper, or Tavily. The current price is returned first; the paid call runs only after confirm and a matching price_version."

const QuoteMessage = "Current published price for this request. No paid upstream call was made. Show this price to the user. A displayed price is not a price lock; the gateway computes the charge. Call this tool again with the same arguments, confirm=true, and this price_version only after the user confirms."
